    "Data": {
      "Ticketid": "HF-1003",
      "Customername": "Priya Nair",
      "Subject": "Duplicate charge showing in Concur",
      "Body": "My corporate card shows the same $84.20 client lunch twice in my Concur expense feed. Do I dispute this with the bank or submit both lines with a note? I don't want to get flagged for double-claiming.",
      "Category": "Billing",
      "Priority": "Low",
      "Rationale": "The KB specifically covers duplicate corporate-card transactions in Concur and says not to submit both lines, mark the duplicate as \"Disputed - duplicate,\" and not contact the bank. Category is Billing because the issue is a duplicate charge; priority is Low because this is a question with a documented process and no user blockage.",
      "Confidence": 0.96,
      "Draftreply": "Hi Priya,\n\nThanks for checking before submitting. For the duplicate $84.20 client lunch showing in your Concur expense feed, please do not submit both lines.\n\n1. In Concur, mark the duplicate transaction line as \"Disputed - duplicate.\"\n2. Do not contact the bank yourself for this corporate-card duplicate.\n3. The duplicate should be removed from your Concur feed within 3 business days, and the bank will reverse the pending charge automatically.\n\nThis will help avoid any appearance of double-claiming while the duplicate is cleared.\n\nRegards,\nHomeFix Supply Support Team"
    }
